### Mod loader

Fabric

### Minecraft version

1.21.1

### Mod version

Jade 15.10.6+fabric (the same trimming code is still present on the current `1.21-fabric` branch, so newer versions are likely affected too)

### Modloader version

Fabric Loader 0.16.x + Fabric API 0.115.0+1.21.1

### Issue description

**Symptom** — a chest that contains "big NBT" items (**written books, filled maps**, …) shows **no items at all** in the tooltip. Chests with ordinary stacks work fine, and there is **no error, no crash, nothing in `latest.log`**. In a world with many chests this looks like "some chests show their contents, some don't".

**Root cause** — `snownee.jade.network.ReceiveDataPacket`:

```java
public static final int MAX_SIZE = 16384;

public static void send(CompoundTag tag, ServerPayloadContext context) {
    int size = tag.getSizeInBytes();
    if (size > 16384) {
        if (spamCount++ < 1) {
            Jade.LOGGER.debug("Data size is too large: {}, max: {}, data: {}", size, 16384, tag);
        }
        int c = 0;
        do {
            if (++c > 10) return;
            removeLargest(tag, 0, 1);   // removes the biggest direct child of the root tag
        } while (tag.getSizeInBytes() > 16384);
    }
    context.sendPacket(new ReceiveDataPacket(tag));
}
```

The item list is stored as **one** child of the root tag (`JadeIds.UNIVERSAL_ITEM_STORAGE`, a `ByteArrayTag` produced by `AccessorImpl.encodeAsNbt`). As soon as the container holds big-NBT items, that tag is by far the largest child — so `removeLargest` **deletes the whole item list** in the first iteration and the loop exits (the rest of the data is tiny). On the client `ItemStorageProvider.append` then finds no `jade:item_storage` key and renders nothing.

Because the only notice is `LOGGER.debug`, users (and pack authors) never see any hint — the data is just gone.

**Real-world evidence** (1.21.1, singleplayer, chest at `119/120,49,-16`, a double chest in the End):

| half | contents | server data | result |
|---|---|---|---|
| right (`120,49,-16`) | 27 ordinary stacks (banners, pumpkins, carrots, …) | small | items shown ✔ |
| left (`119,49,-16`) | 2× `filled_map` + 3× `written_book` (one of them has **44 KB** of `written_book_content`) | **≈46 KB** | **nothing shown** ✖ |

After removing the big book from the left half the tooltip works again, so the trigger really is the data size, not the container/double-chest handling.

**Suggested fix** — any of these would help:

1. Raise `MAX_SIZE`. Vanilla's own payload cap is `ClientboundCustomPayloadPacket.MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE = 1048576` (1 MB) and Jade already reads the tag back with a 2 MB `NbtSizeTracker`, so 16 KB is far more conservative than the transport requires.
2. If a size cap is kept, degrade gracefully instead of deleting the whole item list — e.g. drop only the oversized item components (keep `id` + `count`), or cap the number of items, or send a "contents too large" placeholder.
3. At minimum log at `INFO`/`WARN` when data is dropped, so this is diagnosable from a normal log.

**Local workaround** — since this is a single-player setup I patch the client: a mixin injects at the head of `ReceiveDataPacket.send` and sends the packet directly when `getSizeInBytes() <= 512 KB`, leaving bigger payloads to Jade's original logic. Happy to drop the patch once this is fixed upstream.
